134
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:07,000
and FredXS will detect with the collaborator.

135
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:11,000
And I'll include a couple of these, the Terek examples, request smuggling, cash boiling.

136
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Some of those will use collaborator payloads.

137
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:18,000
And I'll be able to do JWT specific scan checks early on the year.

138
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
And for these particular vulnerabilities, the collaborator was the right tool to use.

139
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
So there's many, many more scan checks which use the collaborator.

140
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
This is just a small sample.

141
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:34,000
So obviously the scanner takes care of many details for you.

142
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
And one of these is the polling associated with the collaborator use.

143
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
So both within individual scan checks and then the key points within the scan itself,

144
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:48,000
the scanner will poll the collaborator, retrieve any interactions relating to its own payloads,

145
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
and then report the relevant issues.

146
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:55,000
In addition to this, there's also background polling which goes on within BIRP when it's running.

147
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:00,000
This is useful for finding deferred issues, deferred interactions.

148
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:05,000
So for example, you can imagine using, sending some payloads on a Friday.

149
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,000
So either manually within the manual tools in BIRP or using the scanner,

150
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:13,000
shut down your project file, go home for the weekend, and over the weekend,

151
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:18,000
some system takes these payloads, triggers interaction with the collaborator server.

152
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:23,000
You come back on the Monday, fire up your project file, and then this background polling will start.

153
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
And then we'll go off to the collaborator, retrieve the interactions.

154
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:30,000
And then in the case of the manual testing report, relevant interactions,

155
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
and the case of the scanner report, the relevant issues.

156
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
So that's a nice capability.

157
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Okay, so this is an example of an issue we've detected using the collaborator.

158
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:48,000
