00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:24,000
So I appreciate this may appear as quite a dry topic to concentrate on, but it's something we get asked on nearly every customer call.

206
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:38,000
The main reason being is if you're currently using a competitor solution, our licensing model is quite unique in the sense that we charge per concurrent scan and not per application or URL.

207
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:48,000
So to clarify, we don't limit you on the number of apps, domains, users, URLs, anything else, only scan concurrency.

208
00:20:48,000 --> 00:21:00,000
So the fact that we license Burp Street Enterprise on scan concurrency or the maximum number of scans you can run at one time, it makes our model extremely flexible.

209
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:09,000
And it's important to note that you can actually also assign and reassign your scans across any websites, applications and URLs.

210
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:18,000
But from this, we're often asked, well, how many concurrent scans do I need if I'm not being charged per application?

211
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:29,000
And in order to best determine how many a customer might require, we ask them to have a think about how many, well, what number of apps do they have and how often do they need to scan them?

212
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Also, whether they have a specific window that they would like to scan in.

213
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:43,000
So for example, they may be restricted to only scan on weekends, overnight, and then finally, whether they have a specific budget in mind.

214
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:54,000
But if we look at an example, so say you have 500 applications across your organization, some may be public facing apps that have daily dev work.

215
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:00,000
So maybe internal apps that are stable and possibly only have work carried out every quarter.

216
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:07,000
But whatever the combination, it's unlikely that you're going to need to be scanning all 500 every day.

217
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:10,000
More realistically, you may be hitting 50 apps per day.

218
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:18,000
And that'll be from a combination of scheduled scans and scans triggered by your CI CD pipeline of choice.

219
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:25,000
So assuming your scan times fit into a working day, you'd only need to purchase 50 concurrent scans.

220
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:31,000
And if you kicked off more scans than you had available, they would just be queued until free.

