391
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
We'll just touch on one last integration, which is CI-CD scanning.

392
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:09,000
I'm going to use the example of Jenkins.

393
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:15,000
With the use of our driver, you can also perform your enterprise scans within your pipelines.

394
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:18,000
So I'm going to give the example of a site-driven scan.

395
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:21,000
I'll just log in here.

396
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:24,000
If we go to configure.

397
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:29,000
So in this example, by adding the driver, we get some additional build steps available within Jenkins.

398
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:32,000
The site-driven scan and the burp scan.

399
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:35,000
So I can add this step to any of my pipelines.

400
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:38,000
And what we're doing here is connecting back to our enterprise server instance.

401
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:43,000
So we've got the URL and the API key for authentication, which is generated from an API user.

402
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:45,000
We've made an enterprise.

403
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:50,000
With the driver installed, we'll get access to our list of sites, our site tree.

404
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:54,000
And we can select which site we want to target as part of this build.

405
00:36:54,000 --> 00:37:00,000
And then we determine when we want the build to fail based on the severities that we're discovering during the scan.

406
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:03,000
So severity and confidence can be set.

407
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:07,000
We can permit a certain number of issues if we've got a certain threshold.

408
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:10,000
And then once that's all configured, we can save.

409
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Anytime that's built, we'll get an API generated scan request back to enterprise.

410
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:19,000
So we jump into enterprise here in our scan list.

411
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:21,000
We can see that that's been received.

412
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:27,000
And then Jenkins through the use of the driver will be able to monitor that scan based on the results we get.

413
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:36,000
We can fail the build if required and we can monitor it in the console.

414
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Okay, folks, that's it in terms of the demo.

