419
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:56,000
And now we'll be rounding this session off with a quick glimpse as to what is left for our 2022 roadmap.

420
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:59,000
So our roadmap is made public on our website.

421
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:10,000
There's a great blog post that documents all of our roadmap items that have been added under our work in progress for both that enterprise pro and scanner.

422
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:17,000
However, I've picked out a few things from our enterprise roadmap that I know some of our customers will be interested in.

423
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:22,000
So first up, we have CI CD in version of control.

424
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:30,000
So this will enable users to start a BurpSuite Enterprise scanning machine in a container controlled by a CI system.

425
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:38,000
So this will make it possible to run scans from within temporary environments, which were not previously accessible by enterprise edition scanning machines.

426
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:44,000
And this will essentially hopefully helps people save on infrastructure costs.

427
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:53,000
In addition to our current methods of billing, we will be enabling users to pay for BurpSuite Enterprise edition scans as and when they use them.

428
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:59,000
So that's further simplifying the process of scanning web portfolios at scale.

429
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:06,000
At present, we have the HTML export capability, which you'll have just seen on the demo that Alex has just run us through.

430
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:21,000
And he also mentioned that we will be enabling users to export scan results as Burp XML, which enables easier integration systems such as Defect Dojo and other vulnerability management tools.

431
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:31,000
And then finally, we will be providing templates containing reference stack implementations for deployment sub BurpSuite Enterprise on a managed Kubernetes cluster.

432
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:34,000
So that's on either GCP or Azure.

433
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:41,000
And for most users, this will greatly simplify the process of deploying Enterprise Edition to these services.

